              Summary
              
                Parthenium hysterophorus
                (Asteraceae), of South American origin, is considered to be one of the world’s most serious invasive plants, invading Australia, Asia and Africa. As part of an international collaborative project, this study attempted to improve the understanding of the geographical distribution of
